  "summary": "TPAP local login of encrypt_type ['4'] cameras: SPAKE2+ (P-256, RFC 9383) pake_register/pake_share with md5/sha256 passcodes and extra_crypt shadows, then an AES-128-CCM binary /stok/ds channel.",
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "tpap.selection",
      "kind": "state_machine",
      "description": "Which login to use. TDP advertises encrypt_type ['4'] and tpap {pake:[2], tls, noc, port:443, user_hash_type}. If tpap.pake is non-empty or encrypt_type contains '4', go straight to TPAP. Otherwise send the v3 step 1; a TPAP-only camera answers -40211 and the client switches to TPAP. A camera that answers pake_register with -40413 + data.encrypt_type ['3'] wants v3.",
      "value": {
        "v3_step1_reply_on_tpap_firmware": -40211,
        "register_reply_wanting_v3": -40413,
        "tdp_fields": [
          "encrypt_type",
          "tpap.pake",
          "tpap.port",
          "tpap.user_hash_type"
        ]
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "jadx",
          "file": "com/tplink/libtapocameranetwork/transport/local/j2.java",
          "line": 277,
          "snippet": "if (pake.contains(2)) {"
        },
        {
          "source": "jadx",
          "file": "com/tplink/libtapocameranetwork/common/CameraErrorCode.java",
          "line": 35,
          "snippet": "MISSING_NECESSARY_PARAMS(-40211),"
        },
